:"closed","created_at":"2025-05-22T16:25:52Z","updated_at":"2026-10-04T16:23:23Z","due_on":null,"closed_at":"2026-01-26T18:09:14Z"},"comments":1,"created_at":"2026-02-09T20:56:43Z","updated_at":"2026-02-10T19:31:45Z","closed_at":"2026-02-10T18:35:49Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/116111","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116111","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116111.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116111.patch","merged_at":"2026-02-10T18:35:49Z"},"body":"*(This is the same as #116067, but targeting the `4.6` branch instead, since that one doesn't make much sense to merge to `master`, with #116041 being the more proper fix there.)*\r\n\r\nFixes #116050.\r\n\r\nThis restores the lower bound of the `total_mass` property of `SoftBody3D` back from the new value of `0.001`, as changed in #108758, to the old value of `0`.\r\n\r\nNote that this is mostly a hack, to accommodate for the [questionable](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116076) implementation of `total_mass` found in the Jolt Physics integration, where it will default to 0 no matter what the inspector says, and which results in the total mass being automatically calculated to 1 kg per point.","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/